# The one place the write address and the read address are paired.
#
# They stay two values because S3 cannot tell you how a bucket is served: a
# CDN, a custom domain and a raw endpoint all front the same keys, and only
# one of them may be the URL consumers use. But they are not independent
# either. A publish verified through an origin that does not front the bucket
# it just wrote to is a green run that shipped nothing — the round trip in
# hack/mirror-model.sh downloads a correct copy of the same pinned model from
# wherever the origin really points, and every digest matches.
#
# So the pair lives here, together, and the workflows refuse a bucket this
# origin is not known to serve unless the caller names its own origin.
# hack/mirror-model.sh itself reads neither: it takes both on the command
# line and knows nothing about Hoop's buckets.
MIRROR_BUCKET=s3://hoopartifacts/alcatraz
MIRROR_ORIGIN=https://hoopartifacts.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/alcatraz
